# Chat Question-and-Answer Core (Cursor)

## Canonical instructions

For project-wide agent discovery, read
[`copilot-instruction.md`](../../.github/copilot-instruction.md). Do not
duplicate policy from that file or from skills. Keep Cursor rules as short
router pointers.

## Skills

When the task touches ChatQnA build, deployment, testing, or API validation,
discover and read the relevant `SKILL.md` under
[`.github/skills/`](../../.github/skills/).
Prefer [`skill-catolog.json`](../../.github/skills/skill-catolog.json) for
routing, but do not assume a fixed list of skill files.

## Cursor workflow

- Prefer the repo's real interfaces: `scripts/setup_env.sh`, Docker Compose,
	Helm chart values, pytest and vitest commands, and REST APIs under
	`/v1/chatqna/...`.
- Run commands in the real environment when possible and investigate failures
	before giving up.
- Create commits or pull requests only when the user explicitly asks.
- Keep edits minimal and follow conventions in the touched area.
